        "Sub-agent delegation enforces max recursion depth, active/total child spawn budgets, parent tenant/caller binding, and narrowed KB/tool/MCP/host scope intersection so prompt-injected tasks cannot escalate privileges beyond the parent run.",
        "Idempotent spawn deduplication verifies both RequestKey and normalized target/task payload equality, rejecting cross-round tool-call ID collisions instead of silently returning stale child runs.",
        "Parent-run lifecycle cleanup cancels in-flight child runs, drains completion queues, and prevents goroutine or lease leaks under concurrent Spawn/Wait/Close (-race)."
      ],
      "findings": [
        {
          "id": "W5-COLLAB-001",
          "severity": "P1",
          "file": "internal/agent/collaboration/runtime.go:305-365, internal/agent/tools/collaboration.go:195-235, internal/agent/tools/exec_context.go:15-55",
          "summary": "Runtime.Spawn returned an existing child record on RequestKey match without checking TargetID/Task equality, and collaborationSpawnTool derived RequestKey without Round/ToolIndex, causing providers that reuse tool_call IDs (e.g. 'call_1') across ReAct rounds to silently alias distinct sub-agent spawns.",
          "regression_test": "TestSpawnRejectsMismatchedRequestKeyReuse, TestCollaborationSpawnAcrossRoundsWithRepeatedToolCallID",
          "commit": "94e890230c2ecc594460bb35937ff496be463407"
        }
